      "summary": "Hard slug-level claim lock for /z-plan and /z-audit-plan preventing silent double-work by concurrent sessions. Orthogonal to the lockless awareness registry (Invariant 1 — registry stays advisory, claim lock is a hard mutex). Thin wrapper scripts/plan-claim.sh over sink-lock.sh; lock path via plan-path.sh:claims_dir(). Holder string: <session_id>::<run_id>::<command>. Acquire exit codes: 0=acquired/self-reentry/disabled, 1=live-peer (holder JSON stdout, TOCTOU/display-only), 2=stale-takeover (we hold, normal post-crash path), 3=corrupt. Heartbeat exit 9=confirmed-lost-claim only (transient read error is heartbeat_error+exit-0, not exit-9). Release always exit-0 (best-effort). Env-only knobs (not TOML keys): Z_HARNESS_CLAIM_TTL_SECS (2700), Z_HARNESS_CLAIM_OVERRIDE (unattended proceed), Z_HARNESS_CLAIM_DISABLE=1 (escape hatch; release is safe no-op). Manual unlock: rm <claims_dir>/<slug>.lock{,.hb.lock}.",
